  "worked_solution": "First, let's swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\nx+10=-6\n$$\n\nTo isolate $x$, we need to perform the *opposite* of adding $10$ to $x,$ which is *subtracting* $10$ from $x.$ Remember to perform the same operation on the right-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+10 & =-6 \\\\ x+10-10 & =-6-10 \\\\ x+0 & =-16 \\\\ x & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$",
